  16:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****   [..]
  17:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****    (#) Enable and configure the peripheral to be connected to the DMA Channel
  18:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        (except for internal SRAM / FLASH memories: no initialization is
  19:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        necessary). Please refer to Reference manual for connection between peripherals
  20:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        and DMA requests .
  21:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  22:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****    (#) For a given Channel, program the required configuration through the following parameters:
  23:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        Transfer Direction, Source and Destination data formats,
  24:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        Circular or Normal mode, Channel Priority level, Source and Destination Increment mode,
  25:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        using HAL_DMA_Init() function.
  26:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  27:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****    (#) Use HAL_DMA_GetState() function to return the DMA state and HAL_DMA_GetError() in case of er
  28:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****        detection.
  29:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  30:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_dma.c ****    (#) Use HAL_DMA_Abort() function to abort the current transfer
